---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SourceList from '../components/SourceList.astro';
import { sourceList } from '../data/sources';
---

<Layout
  title="When expedite is real — FastLicense"
  description="Most collection, lending, money transmitter, and mortgage company licenses have no published paid expedite. Start earlier; do not buy a fake fast-track."
>
  <section class="masthead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Expedite</p>
      <h1>There is usually no skip-the-line window.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        For Cornerstone’s four cores, we did not find a general, regulator-published paid expedite
        that shortens company-license review the way a passport agency sells a faster appointment.
        If a page does not cite one, treat “expedite” as a sales word.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>What is not an expedite</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Submitting through NMLS. That is the filing channel, not a priority queue.</li>
        <li>A statutory 120-day clock. That is an outer bound after completeness, and it can be extended.</li>
        <li>A vendor “fast-track” week range with no regulator citation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What actually moves a date</h2>
      <p>
        File a complete MU1 / state checklist the first time. Authorize every required criminal
        background check before the 180-day fingerprint window dies. Post the bond in the name the
        checklist uses. Answer deficiency letters before the agency withdraws the file.
      </p>
      <p>
        California DRE, on its processing-time page, tells applicants to use eLicensing “for faster
        service” and lists missing course data and fingerprint reports as delay causes. That is a
        process instruction for MLO endorsements, not a paid company-license rush fee.
      </p>

      <h2>When to start earlier</h2>
      <p>
        Start before banking partners, warehouse lines, or a product launch need the license in
        hand. Money-transmitter statutes that use a 120-day complete-application clock still
        require the FBI response to be in the file before that clock starts. A name-check CBC can
        take up to 90 days by NMLS’s own description.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you need a sequenced multi-state calendar, that is operating work —
        <a href="https://cornerstonelicensing.com/contact">ask Cornerstone</a> — not a number this
        directory will invent.
      </p>

      <SourceList sources={sourceList(['ca_dre_times', 'nmls_cbc', 'csbs_mtma_model', 'nmls_checklist'])} />
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
